Subject: [PATCH 04512/11362] [outer-loop] Multi-level deepening: within-game
 L2->L3 self-induction probe NAMES the L2-stall ceiling (win-exemplar floor)

Operator "both" -> Task A (build+run the within-game self-induction probe) + Task B
(packaging audit). This is Task A. Designed via workflow wf_b77c3b40-f11 (4-lens map +
synthesis): the probe COMPOSES existing parts (no new infra) -- reach the solved frontier,
capture the agent's OWN win/non-win grids, induce the next-level goal-energy
(arc_agi3_goal_induction.induce_goal_energy), then (stage 2) search to L3 via
graph_explore_solve_v2 with the L2 prefix + change-location priors, reproduction-gated,
solve_provenance=live_agent_self_discovery.

STAGE-1 RESULT (cd82, decisive): the agent reaches the solved frontier with only ONE
level-completion exemplar (verified: level sequence [0,0,0,0,0,1,...,1] = exactly one
level-up across the 20-label trajectory). induce_goal_energy requires >=2 win grids ->
returned None -> goal re-induction CANNOT FIRE. verdict
complete_self_induction_bounded_no_l3_win_exemplar_floor_n_win_1; adversarial_verify clean.

This NAMES why 15 of 24 games stall at exactly L2: not a search/perception failure, but
the goal-induction operator structurally can't bootstrap from a single win exemplar.
Logged as GAP-4890 (high priority) in ops/verifier_gaps.md: need a single-win-exemplar (or
multi-positive-harvesting) goal-induction operator -- the single binding lever on
multi-level deepening via live self-discovery.

TASK B (separate finding, no commit needed): there is NO free-score packaging win --
reproducible_total_levels=67 is a public-game DEV PROXY that scores ~0 on the hidden
leaderboard (registry's own note); the scored baseline is 0.08. Packaging does not move
the contest score; only the live agent on hidden games does -> Task A is the real lever.

